# Custom merge driver for DERIVED / APPEND-ONLY registry JSON files that every migration PR touches.
# Without this, any migration PR that merges first conflicts EVERY other open migration PR on these
# single shared files, and hand-resolving them then fails `verify:schema-parity` in CI. The json-union
# driver (scripts/git-merge-driver.mjs, registered by scripts/setup-git-merge-drivers.mjs) deep-unions
# both sides automatically so `git merge origin/main` never surfaces a conflict on them. The post-merge
# hook then canonicalizes the schema-parity baseline via `--update` (pure static, no DB).
docs/schema-parity-baseline.json        merge=json-union
db/migrations/.held-migrations.json     merge=json-union
scripts/entity-isolation-allowlist.json merge=json-union

# CONFLICT-TREADMILL KILLER (2026-07-13): every guard/verify PR appends a `verify:*` script to
# package.json and a run-step to locked-guards.yml at the SAME tail anchor, so whichever PR merges
# first conflicts EVERY other open PR on these two files — the endless hand-resolve treadmill.
#   - package.json: the json-union driver deep-unions the scripts object (verified: JSON.parse →
#     JSON.stringify(_,null,2) roundtrips package.json byte-identically, so unchanged content never
#     churns — only the newly-added keys from both sides survive). Driver auto-registered by the
#     `prepare` npm script (scripts/setup-git-merge-drivers.mjs) on every install.
#   - locked-guards.yml: git's built-in `union` driver keeps BOTH sides of an append-only conflict
#     hunk (the guard step list only ever grows at the tail), yielding valid YAML with every branch's
#     steps. (union is line-based — safe here BECAUSE we only ever APPEND guard steps, never edit
#     existing lines; keep it that way.)
package.json                            merge=json-union
.github/workflows/locked-guards.yml     merge=union
